<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Jatprole Samasthan</h1><p class="st-meta">1600 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Kollapur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">One of the leading Telugu samasthans under the Nizams of Hyderabad, ruled by the Velama family of Surabhi from Kollapur.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Jatprole was a hereditary estate held by the Surabhi family, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/velama">Velama</a> chiefs who had served earlier <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telugu-language">Telugu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a> rulers. By about 1600 they held lands in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna-river">Krishna</a> valley, in what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagarkurnool-district">Nagarkurnool district</a>, and kept them under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/golconda-sultanate">Qutb Shahis</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizam-of-hyderabad">Nizams</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>As a samasthan, Jatprole was a tributary estate within <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hyderabad-state">Hyderabad State</a> rather than a separate treaty state, paying peshkash to the Nizam while governing internally through its Raja. Its rulers patronised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telugu-language">Telugu</a> literature and temples, and moved their seat to Kollapur.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>With the annexation of Hyderabad by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in 1948 and the abolition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jagir">jagirs</a> and samasthans soon after, Jatprole ceased to exist. Its lands lie in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telangana">Telangana</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="princely state, 1600 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">princely state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Indian princely states</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:91.54%;width:6.93%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1600 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kollapur</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Telugu</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Jatprole, Kollapur</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1774&amp;focus=jatprole-samasthan" aria-label="Jatprole Samasthan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6815 1579 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Jatprole Samasthan lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7135 1835L7132 1789M7135 1835L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7132 1789h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7135 1835h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7135 1835h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kollapur. <a href="/atlas?year=1774&amp;focus=jatprole-samasthan">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
